  "content": {
    "title": "How to watch, get tickets for Brazil vs. France men's soccer friendly",
    "text": "March 23, 2026Updated March 26, 2026, 12:25 a.m. ETTwo of the most legendary national teams in the world of men's soccer are descending upon Foxboro.Brazil and France are set to face each other in an international friendly at Gillette Stadium at 4 p.m. on Thursday, March 26. The match is part of a four-game friendly series called “Road To 26,” which also features Colombia and Croatia, taking place across the country in preparation of hosting the 2026 FIFA World Cup.This is the first meeting between the multi-time World Cup champions since 2015, when Seleção took down Les Bleus 3-1 in a friendly at the Stade de France in Paris. It’s also a preparation for Gillette Stadium itself, which for sponsorship reasons will be known as Boston Stadium while hosting seven matches, including a quarterfinal, in this summer’s World Cup.France will also get a chance to familiarize itself with Foxboro, as the 2018 World Cup champion and 2022 finalist will be based in Boston this summer, training at Babson College and facing Norway in a highly-anticipated group stage match in Foxboro on June 26.Ahead of kickoff, here's how you can watch the international friendly between Brazil and France.Is the Brazil vs. France friendly match airing on TV?The match is scheduled to air exclusively on ESPN2 and ESPN Deportes. It will also be broadcast in Portuguese over the radio by the New England Revolution's Portuguese language radio partner Nossa Radio USA (WBIX 1260 AM).Are tickets still available for the Brazil vs. France friendly at Gillette Stadium?Yes. As of Monday, March 22, tickets for the match are still available via Ticketmaster starting at $224.64 via a \"verified resale.\"How can I get to Gillette Stadium for the match?General parking for the match will be available for all patrons with tickets as with any other game or event at Gillette Stadium, with lots set to open at noon. For those using a rideshare service such as Uber or Lyft, schedule pick up and drop off at the stadium's designated rideshare location located in Lot 15A, next to Bass Pro Shops.The Massachusetts Bay Transit Authority (MBTA) is also running a specialized commuter rail service for the match. Round trip tickets to and from South Station are available for $30 via the mTicket app with four departures scheduled at 12:45 p.m., 1 p.m., 1:15 p.m. and 1:30 p.m. respectively. All four trains are scheduled to arrive in Foxboro an hour after their departures, with the four return trips set to begin 30 minutes after the conclusion of the match, leaving roughly 15 minutes after each other.",
